8	 * Assigns the owner's {@code householdSize}: the number of owners that belong to the new owner's
9	 * household (share its {@code householdId}), including the owner being created.
10	 *
11	 * <p>Runs within the create transaction after {@link AssignHousehold} (which sets the
12	 * {@code householdId}) and before {@link SaveOwner}, so the count reflects the owners that already
13	 * exist plus this one. An owner with no household (no {@code householdId} — e.g. one created without
14	 * a postcode) is left with a {@code householdSize} of 1, since it belongs to no shared household.
15	 *
16	 * <p>The count is stored on the owner so {@code OwnerMapper} can derive the household membership
17	 * points purely from the owner's own fields, without going back to the database while mapping.
18	 */
19	public class AssignHouseholdSize {
20	
21	    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
22	        String householdId = owner.getHouseholdId();
23	        if (householdId == null || householdId.isBlank()) {
24	            owner.setHouseholdSize(1);
25	            return;
26	        }
27	        int count = 1; // include the owner being created, not yet persisted
28	        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
29	            if (householdId.equals(existing.getHouseholdId())) {
30	                count++;
